[41.885272, "o", "Arrow Library - Date/Time Manipulation Library\r\n\r\nKey Functions to Test:\r\n\r\n1. arrow.get() - Main parsing function\r\n   - Parse various date/time formats from strings\r\n   - Handle timestamps (int, float)\r\n   - Parse datetime objects\r\n   - Handle timezone expressions\r\n   - Test with malformed input, edge cases\r\n\r\n2. arrow.now() / arrow.utcnow() - Current time functions\r\n   - Test with different timezones\r\n\r\n3. Arrow.format() - Formatting functions\r\n   - Format to various string representations\r\n   - Test with different locales\r\n\r\n4. Arrow parsing (parser.py)\r\n   - DateTimeParser.parse() - parse date strings with format strings\r\n   - Test various format tokens\r\n   - Handle edge cases and malformed inputs\r\n\r\n5. Arrow.humanize() - Human-readable time differences\r\n   - Test with different granularities\r\n\r\n6. Arrow arithmetic operations\r\n   - shift(), replace(), floor(), ceil()\r\n   - Range operations\r\n\r\nFuzzing Strategy:\r\n- Focus on get() with random string inputs (most likely to have parsing bugs)\r\n- Test format() "]
