[71.28639, "i", "cat > /app/black/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\nBlack Library - Python Code Formatter\n\nKey Functions to Test:\n\n1. format_str() - Main formatting function\n   - Format Python source code strings\n   - Handle various Python syntax versions\n   - Test with different mode options\n   - Handle malformed Python code\n\n2. format_file_contents() - Format file contents\n   - Format complete Python files\n   - Handle encoding issues\n   - Test with various newline formats\n\n3. format_cell() - Format Jupyter notebook cells\n   - Format individual code cells\n   - Handle IPython magics\n\n4. format_ipynb_string() - Format Jupyter notebooks\n   - Parse and format entire notebooks\n   - Handle notebook metadata\n\n5. decode_bytes() - Decode source bytes\n   - Handle various encodings\n   - Detect newline formats\n\n6. Parsing functions (parsing.py)\n   - lib2to3_parse() - Parse Python code into AST\n   - Handle syntax errors gracefully\n\n7. String handling (strings.py)\n   - normalize_string_quotes()\n   - String prefix handling\n\nFuzzing Strategy:\n"]
[71.286456, "i", "- Focus on format_str() with random Python code snippets\n- Test with malformed/invalid Python syntax\n- Test edge cases in string literals (quotes, escapes, f-strings)\n- Test various Python language features (async, walrus operator, etc.)\n- Include Unicode and encoding edge cases\n- Test with very long lines and deeply nested structures\nEOF\n"]
[71.28658, "o", "cat > /app/black/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\r\n> "]
