[123.1915, "i", "cat > /app/minisgl/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\nMini-SGLang Library - Lightweight LLM Inference Framework\n\nKey Functions to Test:\n\n1. Server API (server/api_server.py)\n   - Request handling for OpenAI-compatible API\n   - /v1/completions endpoint\n   - /v1/chat/completions endpoint\n   - Request validation and parsing\n   - Error handling for malformed requests\n\n2. Tokenizer (tokenizer/)\n   - tokenize() - Tokenize input text\n   - detokenize() - Convert tokens back to text\n   - Handle various text encodings\n   - Handle special tokens and edge cases\n\n3. Scheduler (scheduler/scheduler.py)\n   - Request scheduling logic\n   - Batch management\n   - Cache management\n   - Prefill and decode scheduling\n\n4. Message handling (message/)\n   - Request and response message parsing\n   - Message validation\n   - Handle various message formats\n\n5. Engine (engine/engine.py)\n   - Model inference execution\n   - Sampling strategies\n   - Configuration handling\n\n6. KV Cache (kvcache/)\n   - Cache allocation and management\n   - Radix cach"]
[123.19156, "i", "e operations\n\nFuzzing Strategy:\n- Focus on API server with malformed HTTP requests\n- Test tokenizer with various Unicode inputs and edge cases\n- Test message parsing with invalid JSON and field values\n- Test scheduler with edge case request patterns\n- Include very long inputs, empty inputs, special characters\n- Test with invalid model parameters and configurations\n- Test concurrent request handling\nEOF\n"]
[123.191705, "o", "cat > /app/minisgl/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\r\n> "]
