[151.484612, "o", "UltraJSON (ujson) Library - Fast JSON Encoder/Decoder\r\n\r\nKey Functions to Test:\r\n\r\n1. ujson.dumps() / ujson.encode() - Encode to JSON string\r\n   - Serialize various Python objects (dict, list, str, int, float, bool, None)\r\n   - Handle nested structures\r\n   - Test with ensure_ascii, encode_html_chars options\r\n   - Test with sort_keys, indent options\r\n   - Test with allow_nan for NaN/Infinity values\r\n   - Test with custom default serializer\r\n   - Test with reject_bytes option\r\n\r\n2. ujson.dump() - Encode to file\r\n   - Write JSON to file-like objects\r\n   - Handle encoding options\r\n\r\n3. ujson.loads() / ujson.decode() - Decode from JSON string\r\n   - Parse valid JSON strings\r\n   - Handle various JSON types\r\n   - Handle malformed JSON (should raise JSONDecodeError)\r\n   - Test with bytes and bytearray inputs\r\n   - Handle Unicode and escape sequences\r\n\r\n4. ujson.load() - Decode from file\r\n   - Read and parse JSON from file-like objects\r\n\r\n5. Error handling\r\n   - JSONDecodeError for invalid JSON\r\n   - Handle edge cases "]
[151.484667, "o", "and malformed input\r\n\r\nFuzzing Strategy:\r\n- Focus on loads() with random/malformed JSON strings\r\n- Test with deeply nested structures (stack overflow risks)\r\n- Test with very long strings and numbers\r\n- Test with invalid Unicode sequences\r\n- Test with incomplete JSON (truncated input)\r\n- Test dumps() with circular references (if applicable)\r\n- Test with special float values (NaN, Inf, -Inf)\r\n- Test with various escape sequences and special characters\r\n- Test boundary conditions (empty strings, empty objects/arrays)\r\n- Include non-UTF8 byte sequences\r\n"]
